            <ArticleTitle>Torsion of a rudimentary uterine horn at 22 weeks of gestation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>919-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1447-0756.2010.01435.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rudimentary uterine horn is an uncommon abnormality of the female reproductive tract. Torsion of rudimentary uterine horn in pregnancy is even rarer. A case of successful excision of distorted rudimentary uterine horn in the second trimester, which caused severe abdominal pain, is described. A congenital absence of the right kidney was discovered simultaneously. The pregnancy continued uneventfully until term delivery.</AbstractText>
